[English]

Hi everyone,

I created WMM (Wallpaper Multi-Monitor Manager), a free and open-source wallpaper manager designed specifically for multi-monitor Linux setups.

It originally started as a small applet for Linux Mint, but over time I decided to expand it with more functionality and support for other desktop environments.

The project came from a problem I had with my own setup: I use two 49" monitors together with a third 27" monitor in portrait orientation. I was never completely satisfied with how wallpaper managers handled images with very different monitor orientations, particularly when automatically choosing suitable images or using a single panoramic image across multiple displays.

That eventually became WMM.

I’d like to take this little space to thank Pere for his initial tests on Linux, to Pauki for contributing those wild ideas of his that have really kept me on my toes, and also, a note for Xisco: Arthas not move... yet ;)

Also to Aint, to Senders, and to so many others who have accompanied me on this long journey that has not yet ended...

— Maki

